  "description": "Version 4 of a designed-and-rejected sequence. Version 2 with one change: a claimed square can be claimed back. Its designer rejected it for a reason that is about incentives rather than rules -- taking an opponent's square swings the count by two while claiming a blank one swings it by one, so 'you never want to color in a blank square unless you're forced to', the blank count stops falling and the game never gets closer to finishing. The one-way process is still in the rules; nobody uses it.",
